SCPLAN 1
plan windows-first-host
summary Make the resident Windows app the machine-local orchestration authority while keeping worker backends replaceable.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-WINDOWS-FIRST
intent REQ-MCP-CONTROL-PLANE

task app-project-registry
size small
title add machine-local project registry
instruction Persist known project roots and the last active project in machine-local application state; do not move project authority out of .statefulclanker.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-ACTIVE-PROJECT
capability-profile coding
tool-deny mcp.*
retrieve src/StatefulClanker.Tray/*
retrieve lib/StatefulClanker.Integrations.ps1
accept project registry survives application restart
accept project-local durable state remains under the project root
accept missing project paths remain explicit
end

task app-active-project
size small
title restore and expose the active project
depends app-project-registry
instruction Restore the last active project on startup and make project switching explicit to the UI/control plane.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-ACTIVE-PROJECT
capability-profile coding
accept existing last active project is restored
accept missing last active project produces a no-active-project state
accept no other project is silently substituted
end

task mcp-dual-era
size medium
title serve legacy and modern MCP from one resident authority
depends app-active-project
instruction Keep legacy initialize-era compatibility while serving stateless MCP 2026-07-28 requests and modern subscription wakeups from the same resident endpoint.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-MCP-CONTROL-PLANE
capability-profile coding
retrieve mcp/*
accept legacy clients retain initialize-era behavior
accept modern requests require per-request protocol/capability metadata
accept modern HTTP routing headers are validated
accept stdio forwarding preserves the incoming protocol era
end

task worker-capabilities-ui
size medium
title expose machine worker capabilities in the Windows app
depends app-active-project
instruction Expose machine allow/deny policy, reusable capability profiles, external MCP worker sources, and active-project policy access without creating a second authorization authority.
source human:h-0001
intent REQ-WINDOWS-FIRST
capability-profile coding
retrieve src/StatefulClanker.Tray/*
retrieve lib/StatefulClanker.WorkerPolicy.ps1
accept app edits the same worker-capabilities.json consumed by runtime
accept source-specific grants cannot broaden unrelated capability namespaces
accept project policy remains tighten-only
end
